               <p xml:id="idm165">The cantata was composed for the feast in memory of the national-liberal politician Orla Lehmann, who had died on 13 September 1870. It was arranged by Dansk Folkeforening (Danish People's Society) taking place on 26 November 1870. The society had been founded in 1865 with the purpose of "strengthening and developing the national spirit and awareness so that it would pervade our society and official life.". With the popular Orla Lehmann as chairman the Society appealed to a lot of people, but was dissolved after his death five years later. Originally the feast should had taken place on 5 November; however, Hartmann did not get the text for the cantata until 25 October.</p>
            </history>
